{"seq":null,"commit_to":{"owner":"pertson-labs","repo":"e2e-expert-repo","branch":"live/some-other-title-that-should-not-win--eb1db9f90d1c"},"doc_stem":"2026-08-25-1-derive-id-explicit-override","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":7,"spec_hash":"c834f46b2b0c"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-7c144fcd","payload":{"expand_iris":["ns__Strategy","ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping","ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst"],"focus":"Some Other Title That Should Not Win — minimal placeholder document with no substantive content, reviewers, or decisions","rationale":"The document is a near-empty placeholder (title + 'Body.'), so no graph area substantively overlaps with its content. The perspective returned only a focus-scoped tail surfacing Decision_KnowledgeMapping under Strategy; I expanded Strategy and its two children (KnowledgeMapping, DiagnosticFirst) to confirm whether any decision or position could plausibly bear on this document. None does — the document contains no concepts, decisions, or themes that connect to the graph. I deliberately did not expand further since there is nothing in the document to anchor additional expansions to.","n8n_execution_id":"145444","expansion_count":3,"context":"# Perspective — pertson-labs/e2e-expert-repo @ a6ee0b5b62511c03200d600c746c2131f55281b1\npin: a733ecab1c90ff1f2cd5877de7ba1df11572c475\n\nSections, stable-first: (1) THE MAP — the richest areas at steering grain; (2) AREA INDEX — every other area, named, one line each; (3) ACTIVE SURFACE — recent + load-bearing witnesses; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map and index never vary with your focus; your per-call material is at the end.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nDeciding where to go: each mapped area's narration tells you the SPAN of what lives under it; the area index names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# Focus: Some Other Title That Should Not Win — minimal placeholder document with no substantive content, reviewers, or decisions (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\n### ns__Strategy\n\nchildren (witness depth):\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst  (already in your context)\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst, ^ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping, ^ns__Strategy\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"a733ecab1c90ff1f2cd5877de7ba1df11572c475","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":2744},"live_run_id":"eb1db9f90d1c","at":"2026-08-25T10:11:17Z"}
